docs/PAYLOAD_CONTRACTS.md:3956:- DOCX artifacts normally use the styled `python-docx` renderer. When that optional dependency is unavailable, the pipeline emits a minimal but valid DOCX package containing the same pleading text, affidavit text, section headings, grouped factual-allegation headings, claim-support gaps, and handoff content so document generation continues to consume and preserve validated support state instead of failing the export.
docs/PAYLOAD_CONTRACTS.md:3957:- `drafting_readiness.claims[*].review_url`, `drafting_readiness.claims[*].review_context`, and `drafting_readiness.claims[*].review_intent` are added by the document API layer so clients can deep-link into the claim-support review surface without reconstructing query parameters themselves.

